## How to Test

1. Restart the backend: `npm run dev` in [Backend/](file:///c:/Users/Computer%20Arena/Documents/webDev%20works/full%20stack/SkillSync/Frontend/src/config/runtime.js#30-36)
2. Ensure frontend is running: `npm run dev` in `Frontend/`
3. Log in as a **recruiter**
4. Navigate to the **Applicants** page
5. Click the floating ✨ button (bottom-right corner)
6. Try: *"Who are my top candidates?"* or click a quick prompt
7. Verify AI responds with applicant-specific data

## Key Design Decisions

- **Context-window stuffing** over vector DB — recruiter pools are bounded, Gemini's 1M token window handles it easily
- **Stateless API** — conversation history sent from frontend, backend doesn't store sessions
- **Resume text capped at 3000 chars** per applicant to stay well within token limits even with many applicants
- **Shared [pdfUtils.js](file:///c:/Users/Computer%20Arena/Documents/webDev%20works/full%20stack/SkillSync/Backend/utils/pdfUtils.js)** — avoids code duplication between [aiService.js](file:///c:/Users/Computer%20Arena/Documents/webDev%20works/full%20stack/SkillSync/Backend/services/aiService.js) and [ragService.js](file:///c:/Users/Computer%20Arena/Documents/webDev%20works/full%20stack/SkillSync/Backend/services/ragService.js)
